    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d494-a2">

                <pb facs="0652" n="540" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg540"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 2]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Howard of
                        Liberia to the American Chargé</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bundy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 19, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am in receipt of your communication of
                    the 17th instant informing this Government that the Government of the United
                    States had established, through its Treasury, a credit of $5,000,000 in favor of
                    Liberia. In reply, I take the opportunity to request you to be good enough to
                    convey to the Government of the United States my most grateful sentiments of
                    appreciation, as well as those of the Government and people of Liberia, for its
                    prompt and generous response to the earnest appeal of the Republic for the
                    financial aid so urgently needed.</p>
                <p>This benevolent action on the part of the United States, taken at a moment when
                    the Republic is confronted with very grave problems arising from its financial
                    embarrassment due to war conditions, has profoundly impressed the Liberian
                    people with the cordial good will and sympathetic interest of the Government of
                    the United States toward the welfare and perpetuity of Liberia.</p>
                <p>Cordially and sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">D. E. Howard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
